WordPress 6.x. Core already answers an unknown URL with 404 and loads the theme's 404.php (then index.php). This recipe adds: the themed template with a nav landmark and a root link, noindex on 404/410, 410 for retired paths, a real 404 for an unknown value of a custom query var, 503 instead of a soft 404 when the database fails mid-request (every 404 re-checks the database with SELECT 1), and the two drop-ins WordPress loads when it cannot connect to the database (wp-content/db-error.php) or hits a fatal PHP error (wp-content/php-error.php). Drop-ins run without the theme, so they are static HTML: copy your header/nav/footer markup into them. Ensure the theme's header.php prints a <nav> (wp_nav_menu with container 'nav', or a literal one).
