WordPress 6.x. The form posts to admin-post.php (works without JavaScript); the nonce (wp_nonce_field / wp_verify_nonce) is the CSRF check, a transient keyed by a salted hash of the IP is the rate limit, a visually hidden text field is the honeypot. Success (303 redirect) only follows a wp_mail() that returned true; false becomes a 502. wp_mail() uses PHP mail() unless SMTP is configured, so set up a real SMTP/provider plugin or the "sent" message is a lie. A nonce on a page cached for more than 12 hours fails (403): exclude the contact page from the page cache. Behind a proxy REMOTE_ADDR is the proxy; map the real client IP at the server first.
